# Build the physical compatibility ledger

## Scope and existing evidence

Record exact model, firmware, adapter tier, transport, paper, pen, usable area,
settings, evidence, known limitations, and last acceptance date.

Current executable evidence now freezes that compatibility record without
claiming support for any untested hardware. Exact model, firmware, transport,
adapter tier, paper, pen, usable area, settings, acceptance evidence, known
limitations, and last acceptance date remain caller-owned values tied to one
combination. Hardware probing, compatibility admission, persistence, expiry or
recertification policy, and physical support claims remain open.

## One finite, explicitly unverified model entry

**Inputs:** declared exact model, observed firmware, transport and adapter
tier, physical page/pen setup, settings, dated dry-run evidence and a human
acceptance decision. **Output:** an append-only profile-scoped record with
`Candidate`, `Verified` or `Unsupported` status and a blocking refusal
reason, not a device-access grant. Unknown facts remain `Unknown`.

**Worked hypothetical entry (not a support claim):**

| Field | Example record value |
| --- | --- |
| Model | AxiDraw V3 (vendor-listed CLI family) |
| Firmware | `EXAMPLE-NOT-REAL-1` (invented test ID) |
| Transport | USB (proposed, disconnected) |
| Adapter tier | `CandidateOnly` |
| Paper and pen | A4 blank, one pen, no actual sample |
| Usable area | `Unknown` (nominal A4 is not calibration) |
| Settings | CLI model 1, strict stroke ordering 4 |
| Evidence | `TheoryOnly`, no dry-run or USB test |
| Date | 2026-11-02 (record design date, not acceptance date) |
| Last physical acceptance | `None` |
| Known limits | No firmware, origin, axes, clamp or pen measurements |

**Evaluation rule:** the pair `(model, firmware)` is immutable identity and
the transport, selected pen, paper mount, calibration, CLI version and
physical capability tier are part of the qualification key. The ledger may
record a hypothetical combination but never promote it to `Verified` from
an offline storyboard alone. A future verified entry must retain source of
model/firmware observations, observer, date, trace, limits and fail result.

**Refusal example:** `PlanForPlot` with this entry must return
`NoVerifiedHardwareCombination` even if its theoretical dimensions fit.
An altered firmware, pen, mount, command mode or calibration invalidates a
previous real acceptance for that changed combination. Do not infer a
firmware version or last physical acceptance date from today's record.

**Assumptions and risks:** vendor lists AxiDraw V3 as an eligible CLI family
(https://axidraw.com/doc/cli_api/), but this repository has no device
probing, persisted ledger verification, timed recertification, operator
training evidence or physical certification. The table is deliberately
unusable to authorize a live plot.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** theoretical ledger example, 2026-11-02, with invented firmware ID.
- **Delivered:** one dated model/firmware/transport candidate, settings,
  explicit missing evidence, limitations, and authorization refusal.
- **Unavailable:** real model/firmware observations, physical compatibility
  decision, live execution, or recertification.
